he ligands = 18 e.","lk":[{"h":"Counting rules","l":[["Green & Parkin, J. Chem. Educ. 2014, 91, 807","https://doi.org/10.1021/ed400504f"]]}]},{"s":"tmc","k":"Electron count","a":"How many valence electrons does Mn have?","o":[{"x":"18 e"},{"x":"17 e"},{"x":"19 e"},{"x":"20 e"}],"t":"Hexacarbonylmanganese(I)","f":"[Mn(CO)₆]⁺","fig":{"m":2305},"ex":"Covalent count: Mn (group 7) 7 e; 6 × CO (L) 12 e; the 1+ charge removes 1 e: 18 e. Ionic count: the ligands carry no charge and the complex has a 1+ charge, so the metal is Mn(I), d⁶; d⁶ + 12 e from the ligands = 18 e. The positive charge removes one electron in the neutral count.","lk":[{"h":"Counting rules","l":[["Green & Parkin, J. Chem. Educ. 2014, 91, 807","https://doi.org/10.1021/ed400504f"]]}]},{"s":"tmc","k":"Oxidation state","a":"What is the oxidation state of Mn?","o":[{"x":"+1"},{"x":"+2"},{"x":"0"},{"x":"−1"}],"t":"Hexacarbonylmanganese(I)","f":"[Mn(CO)₆]⁺","fig":{"m":2305},"ex":"Covalent count: Mn (group 7) 7 e; 6 × CO (L) 12 e; the 1+ charge removes 1 e: 18 e. Ionic count: the ligands carry no charge and the complex has a 1+ charge, so the metal is Mn(I), d⁶; d⁶ + 12 e from the ligands = 18 e. The positive charge removes one electron in the neutral count.","lk":[{"h":"Counting rules","l":[["Green & Parkin, J. Chem. Educ. 2014, 91, 807","https://doi.org/10.1021/ed400504f"]]}]},{"s":"tmc","k":"dⁿ count","a":"What is the dⁿ count of Mn?","o":[{"x":"d⁶"},{"x":"d⁵"},{"x":"d⁷"},{"x":"d⁴"}],"t":"Hexacarbonylmanganese(I)","f":"[Mn(CO)₆]⁺","fig":{"m":2305},"ex":"Covalent count: Mn (group 7) 7 e; 6 × CO (L) 12 e; the 1+ charge removes 1 e: 18 e. Ionic count: the ligands carry no charge and the complex has a 1+ charge, so the metal is Mn(I), d⁶; d⁶ + 12 e from the ligands = 18 e. The positive charge removes one electron in the neutral count.","lk":[{"h":"Counting rules","l":[["Green & Parkin, J. Chem. Educ. 2014, 91, 807","https://doi.org/10.1021/ed400504f"]]}]},{"s":"tmc","k":"Geometry","a":"What shape is it?","o":[{"