 the ligands = 18 e.","lk":[{"h":"Counting rules","l":[["Green & Parkin, J. Chem. Educ. 2014, 91, 807","https://doi.org/10.1021/ed400504f"]]}]},{"s":"tmc","k":"dⁿ count","a":"What is the dⁿ count of Ni?","o":[{"x":"d¹⁰"},{"x":"d⁹"},{"x":"d⁸"}],"t":"Tricarbonyl(triphenylphosphine)nickel","f":"Ni(CO)₃(PPh₃)","fig":{"m":2321},"ex":"Covalent count: Ni (group 10) 10 e; 1 × PPh₃ (L) 2 e; 3 × CO (L) 6 e: 18 e. Ionic count: the ligands carry no charge and the complex is neutral, so the metal is Ni(0), d¹⁰; d¹⁰ + 8 e from the ligands = 18 e.","lk":[{"h":"Counting rules","l":[["Green & Parkin, J. Chem. Educ. 2014, 91, 807","https://doi.org/10.1021/ed400504f"]]}]},{"s":"tmc","k":"Geometry","a":"What shape is it?","o":[{"x":"Tetrahedral"},{"x":"Square planar"},{"x":"Trigonal bipyramidal"},{"x":"Linear"}],"t":"Tricarbonyl(triphenylphosphine)nickel","f":"Ni(CO)₃(PPh₃)","fig":{"m":2321},"ex":"Tetrahedral. Covalent count: Ni (group 10) 10 e; 1 × PPh₃ (L) 2 e; 3 × CO (L) 6 e: 18 e. Ionic count: the ligands carry no charge and the complex is neutral, so the metal is Ni(0), d¹⁰; d¹⁰ + 8 e from the ligands = 18 e.","lk":[{"h":"Counting rules","l":[["Green & Parkin, J. Chem. Educ. 2014, 91, 807","https://doi.org/10.1021/ed400504f"]]}]},{"s":"tmc","k":"Electron count","a":"How many valence electrons does Mo have?","o":[{"x":"18 e"},{"x":"17 e"},{"x":"19 e"},{"x":"16 e"}],"t":"Tris(acetonitrile)molybdenum tricarbonyl","f":"fac-Mo(CO)₃(MeCN)₃","fig":{"m":2322},"ex":"Covalent count: Mo (group 6) 6 e; 3 × CO (L) 6 e; 3 × MeCN (L) 6 e: 18 e. Ionic count: the ligands carry no charge and the complex is neutral, so the metal is Mo(0), d⁶; d⁶ + 12 e from the ligands = 18 e. A source of Mo(CO)₃: the acetonitriles are easily replaced.","lk":[{"h":"Counting rules","l":[["Green & Parkin, J. Chem. Educ. 2014, 91, 807","https://doi.org/10.1021/ed400504f"]]}]},{"s":"tmc","k":"Oxidation state","a":"What is the oxidation state of Mo?","o":[{"x":"0"},{"x":"+1"},{"x":"−1"},{"x":"+2"}],"t":"Tris(acetonitrile