e)chromium cation","f":"[(η⁶-C₆H₆)₂Cr]⁺","fig":{"m":2331},"ex":"Covalent count: Cr (group 6) 6 e; 2 × η⁶-C₆H₆ (L₃) 12 e; the 1+ charge removes 1 e: 17 e. Ionic count: the ligands carry no charge and the complex has a 1+ charge, so the metal is Cr(I), d⁵; d⁵ + 12 e from the ligands = 17 e.","lk":[{"h":"Counting rules","l":[["Green & Parkin, J. Chem. Educ. 2014, 91, 807","https://doi.org/10.1021/ed400504f"]]}]},{"s":"tmc","k":"Electron count","a":"How many valence electrons does Fe have?","o":[{"x":"18 e"},{"x":"19 e"},{"x":"17 e"},{"x":"20 e"}],"t":"Cyclopentadienyl(benzene)iron cation","f":"[CpFe(η⁶-C₆H₆)]⁺","fig":{"m":2332},"ex":"Covalent count: Fe (group 8) 8 e; 1 × Cp (L₂X) 5 e; 1 × η⁶-C₆H₆ (L₃) 6 e; the 1+ charge removes 1 e: 18 e. Ionic count: the ligands carry a charge of −1 in all and the complex has a 1+ charge, so the metal is Fe(II), d⁶; d⁶ + 12 e from the ligands = 18 e.","lk":[{"h":"Counting rules","l":[["Green & Parkin, J. Chem. Educ. 2014, 91, 807","https://doi.org/10.1021/ed400504f"]]}]},{"s":"tmc","k":"Oxidation state","a":"What is the oxidation state of Fe?","o":[{"x":"+2"},{"x":"+3"},{"x":"+1"},{"x":"0"}],"t":"Cyclopentadienyl(benzene)iron cation","f":"[CpFe(η⁶-C₆H₆)]⁺","fig":{"m":2332},"ex":"Covalent count: Fe (group 8) 8 e; 1 × Cp (L₂X) 5 e; 1 × η⁶-C₆H₆ (L₃) 6 e; the 1+ charge removes 1 e: 18 e. Ionic count: the ligands carry a charge of −1 in all and the complex has a 1+ charge, so the metal is Fe(II), d⁶; d⁶ + 12 e from the ligands = 18 e.","lk":[{"h":"Counting rules","l":[["Green & Parkin, J. Chem. Educ. 2014, 91, 807","https://doi.org/10.1021/ed400504f"]]}]},{"s":"tmc","k":"dⁿ count","a":"What is the dⁿ count of Fe?","o":[{"x":"d⁶"},{"x":"d⁵"},{"x":"d⁷"},{"x":"d⁸"}],"t":"Cyclopentadienyl(benzene)iron cation","f":"[CpFe(η⁶-C₆H₆)]⁺","fig":{"m":2332},"ex":"Covalent count: Fe (group 8) 8 e; 1 × Cp (L₂X) 5 e; 1 × η⁶-C₆H₆ (L₃) 6 e; the 1+ charge removes 1 e: 18 e. Ionic count: the ligands carry a charge of −1 in all and the complex has a 1+ charge,