400504f"]]}]},{"s":"tmc","k":"Electron count","a":"How many valence electrons does W have?","o":[{"x":"18 e"},{"x":"17 e"},{"x":"19 e"},{"x":"16 e"}],"t":"Fischer carbene","f":"(CO)₅W=C(OMe)Ph","fig":{"m":2415},"ex":"Covalent count: W (group 6) 6 e; 1 × =C(OMe)Ph (L) 2 e; 5 × CO (L) 10 e: 18 e. Ionic count: the ligands carry no charge and the complex is neutral, so the metal is W(0), d⁶; d⁶ + 12 e from the ligands = 18 e. A Fischer carbene is a neutral 2-electron L ligand: W(0).","lk":[{"h":"Counting rules","l":[["Green & Parkin, J. Chem. Educ. 2014, 91, 807","https://doi.org/10.1021/ed400504f"]]}]},{"s":"tmc","k":"Oxidation state","a":"What is the oxidation state of W?","o":[{"x":"0"},{"x":"+1"},{"x":"−1"},{"x":"−2"}],"t":"Fischer carbene","f":"(CO)₅W=C(OMe)Ph","fig":{"m":2415},"ex":"Covalent count: W (group 6) 6 e; 1 × =C(OMe)Ph (L) 2 e; 5 × CO (L) 10 e: 18 e. Ionic count: the ligands carry no charge and the complex is neutral, so the metal is W(0), d⁶; d⁶ + 12 e from the ligands = 18 e. A Fischer carbene is a neutral 2-electron L ligand: W(0).","lk":[{"h":"Counting rules","l":[["Green & Parkin, J. Chem. Educ. 2014, 91, 807","https://doi.org/10.1021/ed400504f"]]}]},{"s":"tmc","k":"dⁿ count","a":"What is the dⁿ count of W?","o":[{"x":"d⁶"},{"x":"d⁵"},{"x":"d⁷"},{"x":"d⁴"}],"t":"Fischer carbene","f":"(CO)₅W=C(OMe)Ph","fig":{"m":2415},"ex":"Covalent count: W (group 6) 6 e; 1 × =C(OMe)Ph (L) 2 e; 5 × CO (L) 10 e: 18 e. Ionic count: the ligands carry no charge and the complex is neutral, so the metal is W(0), d⁶; d⁶ + 12 e from the ligands = 18 e. A Fischer carbene is a neutral 2-electron L ligand: W(0).","lk":[{"h":"Counting rules","l":[["Green & Parkin, J. Chem. Educ. 2014, 91, 807","https://doi.org/10.1021/ed400504f"]]}]},{"s":"tmc","k":"Geometry","a":"What shape is it?","o":[{"x":"Octahedral"},{"x":"Trigonal prismatic"},{"x":"Square planar"},{"x":"Square pyramidal"}],"t":"Fischer carbene","f":"(CO)₅W=C(OMe)Ph","fig":{"m":2415},"ex":"Octahedral. Covalent count: W (g