m the ligands = 16 e.","lk":[{"h":"Counting rules","l":[["Green & Parkin, J. Chem. Educ. 2014, 91, 807","https://doi.org/10.1021/ed400504f"]]}]},{"s":"tmc","k":"dⁿ count","a":"What is the dⁿ count of Mn?","o":[{"x":"d⁰"},{"x":"d¹"},{"x":"d²"},{"x":"d³"}],"t":"Permanganate","f":"[MnO₄]⁻","fig":{"m":2420},"ex":"Covalent count: Mn (group 7) 7 e; 4 × O (X₂) 8 e; the 1− charge adds 1 e: 16 e. Ionic count: the ligands carry a charge of −8 in all and the complex has a 1− charge, so the metal is Mn(VII), d⁰; d⁰ + 16 e from the ligands = 16 e.","lk":[{"h":"Counting rules","l":[["Green & Parkin, J. Chem. Educ. 2014, 91, 807","https://doi.org/10.1021/ed400504f"]]}]},{"s":"tmc","k":"Geometry","a":"What shape is it?","o":[{"x":"Tetrahedral"},{"x":"Square planar"},{"x":"Linear"},{"x":"Trigonal planar"}],"t":"Permanganate","f":"[MnO₄]⁻","fig":{"m":2420},"ex":"Tetrahedral. Covalent count: Mn (group 7) 7 e; 4 × O (X₂) 8 e; the 1− charge adds 1 e: 16 e. Ionic count: the ligands carry a charge of −8 in all and the complex has a 1− charge, so the metal is Mn(VII), d⁰; d⁰ + 16 e from the ligands = 16 e.","lk":[{"h":"Counting rules","l":[["Green & Parkin, J. Chem. Educ. 2014, 91, 807","https://doi.org/10.1021/ed400504f"]]}]},{"s":"tmc","k":"Electron count","a":"How many valence electrons does Os have?","o":[{"x":"16 e"},{"x":"17 e"},{"x":"15 e"},{"x":"18 e"}],"t":"Nitridotetrachloroosmate","f":"[OsNCl₄]⁻","fig":{"m":2421},"ex":"Covalent count: Os (group 8) 8 e; 1 × N (X₃) 3 e; 4 × Cl (X) 4 e; the 1− charge adds 1 e: 16 e. Ionic count: the ligands carry a charge of −7 in all and the complex has a 1− charge, so the metal is Os(VI), d²; d² + 14 e from the ligands = 16 e. The nitride is an X3 ligand.","lk":[{"h":"Counting rules","l":[["Green & Parkin, J. Chem. Educ. 2014, 91, 807","https://doi.org/10.1021/ed400504f"]]}]},{"s":"tmc","k":"Oxidation state","a":"What is the oxidation state of Os?","o":[{"x":"+6"},{"x":"+5"},{"x":"+7"},{"x":"+4"}],"t":"Nitridotetrachloroosmate","f":"[OsNCl₄]⁻","f